## Documentation namespace

`docs/_internal/` is the agent-facing reasoning record. Its structure mirrors the analysis:

| Output kind | Path |
|-------------|------|
| scientific framing | `docs/_internal/scientific-context.md`, if present |
| stage session | `docs/_internal/<stage-stem>/session.md` |
| stage reasoning | `docs/_internal/<stage-stem>/<topic>.md` |
| cross-stage session | `docs/_internal/_project/session.md` |
| cross-stage reasoning | `docs/_internal/_project/<topic>.md` |
| a phased plan | `docs/_internal/_project/plans/<date-slug>/` as `00_INDEX.md` + `NN_<slug>.md` |

Scope is the only structure here: one directory per stage, plus `_project/` for what
spans them. Create each directory with its first real file, and update `session.md` in
place — an in-place update keeps one current record instead of a dated pile, so write it
knowing it replaces what was there.

**One-way reference rule:** public `docs/` must NOT reference `_internal/` paths.

